-- URL ATTRIBUTE NEEDS A URL ------------------------------------ main.kl  K1613

This hole fills a URL attribute (such as `href` or `src`), so its value must be a `Url`, not a `String`. A string could be a `javascript:` link.

3│     let page = html"""<a href="{home}">home</a>"""
                                   ^^^^

Help: Build the link with a `url"..."` literal, or parse text with `Url.parse(s)`, which refuses `javascript:`, `data:` and `vbscript:`.

Learn more: kalam explain K1613
